/*
 * Declares the CmpClassTypeOperatorValue class.
 *
 * CmpClassTypeOperatorValue represents the class-type comparison operator,
 * written as:
 *
 *        a of A
 *
 * where the left operand is a value of a class type, and the right operand is a
 * class reference. The operator evaluates to a boolean indicating whether the
 * runtime type of the left operand is compatible with (or derived from) the
 * class referenced on the right.
 *
 * This operator is used for type-introspection expressions and cannot be a full
 * literal, since its result depends on runtime type information.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::class_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/class_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2024-04-10
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
